# The server clones themselves are NOT tracked. They are 24 upstream repos with
# their own .git directories plus ~10GB of regenerable build output (node_modules,
# target/, venvs). Nesting them in this repo would give broken gitlinks and commit
# artifacts that rebuild anyway.
#
# What IS tracked is servers.json — every upstream URL and the exact commit in use —
# and setup.sh, which reconstructs the fleet from it. That is the part worth backing
# up: ~50KB that restores 12GB reproducibly.
servers/
